asteroids are important for two reasons  they contain lots of valuable natural  resources and they have the power to  kill everything on earth it's for both  of these reasons that nASA has created  the asteroid hundred contest you can win  up to 35 thousand dollars if you can  come up with a new and improved  algorithm to track and follow asteroids  currently NASA's only able to track  about 1% of all the asteroids in our  solar system that means there could be a  world killing asteroid headed for us  right now and we wouldn't even know it  and we've had a couple of close calls  recently in 2013 a rogue space rock  missed us by only a few thousand miles  closer than some communication  satellites and on the very same day an  asteroid streaked into the atmosphere  over Russia and exploded with the force  of an atomic bomb that asteroid was just  50 feet across an asteroid one mile wide  cue the aerosmith because things are  about to get all cataclysmic hence the  asteroid hunter contest obviously it  would be better to find these things  before there is a planet threatening  event but it's important to note that  NASA's partner in the contest Planetary  Resources is hunting asteroids for an  entirely different reason prophet turns  out that many asteroids are loaded with  precious minerals which means that  crowd-sourced asteroid detection is not  only a good way to prevent mass  extinction but also a good way to make a  buck
 

